{"id":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#lem:chow-iii-g53-distance-derivative","title":"lem:chow-iii-g53-distance-derivative","path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry.md","line":405,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry.tex#lem:chow-iii-g53-distance-derivative","uses":["[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#def:chow-iii-g35-g36-aleksandrov]]","[[references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry#def:chow-iii-g50-exponential-cut-locus]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/ChowEtAl/blueprint/src/chapters/appg-elementary-metric-geometry.tex","label":"lem:chow-iii-g53-distance-derivative","line":567,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[First variation of distance]\n\\label{lem:chow-iii-g53-distance-derivative}\n\\source{chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0431}\n\\uses{def:chow-iii-g35-g36-aleksandrov, def:chow-iii-g50-exponential-cut-locus}\n\\dcref{appG:G.53}\\group{Semi-concavity}\n\nIf $\\alpha$ is a minimal geodesic from $q$ to $p$, $\\beta$ is unit speed from\n$q$, and $p\\notin C(q)$, then\n\\[\n\\left.\\frac{d}{dt^+}\\right|_{0}d(p,\\beta(t))=-\\cos\\angle_q(\\alpha,\\beta).\n\\]\n\\end{lemma}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[First variation of distance] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a63686f772d6969692d6735332d64697374616e63652d64657269766174697665\"></span> <span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">chow-et-al-ricci-flow-part-iii:page-0431</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FChowEtAl%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fappg-elementary-metric-geometry%23def%3Achow-iii-g35-g36-aleksandrov\">↗ def:chow-iii-g35-g36-aleksa